and lets your app retrieve normally   nothing is inserted or removed from
your storage.

The bundled standard dataset is a generic, cross-app benchmark   it is
almost never a corpus match for YOUR app. For this mode to produce
meaningful retrieval-dependent scores (ContextualPrecision/Recall/
Relevancy, Faithfulness), point GOLDENS at your own goldens file instead,
written against what's really in your corpus:

    GOLDENS = load_standard_dataset(
        task_type="{task_type}", ci_stage="{ci_stage}",
        dataset_path="path/to/your_goldens.jsonl",
    )

Only reach for the shared dataset + a temporary seed/teardown of its
`context` passages when you deliberately want to run the generic
benchmark against an app whose corpus doesn't already cover it (e.g. a
throwaway CI corpus). That's a different, opt-in generator:

    elyaeval init --task-type {task_type} --corpus-mode seeded

